# 365 MB of source books, moved to R2 and Internet Archive on 2026-08-23. They were
# shipping through Pages while also being the largest churning blobs in the git pack.
# books.json now points `file` and `markdownFile` at https://data.civgraph.net/..., so
# nothing resolves against these paths any more; check:book-files verifies every remote
# URL is on that host and under an allowlisted prefix.
#   markdown    213 MB  66 Hansard OCR volumes 1921-1945
#   legislation 152 MB  13 NI Acts and SRO PDFs 1921-1932
data/books/markdown/
data/books/legislation/
data/downloads/
OSNI original maps/
data/maps/osni-originals/*.kml
LocalAuthorities_NationalStatutoryBoundaries_Ungeneralised_2024_-2978313920612481790.geojson

# Map data — served from R2 (data.civgraph.net)
data/census/
# Semantic graph shards: 4,604 files, 1.96 GB, served through
# functions/data/graph/[[path]].js. This exclusion is what MAKES that Function
# run. Cloudflare Pages serves a matching static asset in preference to a
# Function, so while these files were deployed the proxy was inert -- it was
# deployed on 2026-08-12 and observably never invoked, because the committed
# copy shadowed it. Re-deploying data/graph would silently disable the proxy
# again, with no error anywhere: the site would keep working, just from the
# wrong source and against the Pages file budget.
data/graph/

# Browse indexes and detail pages: 2,386 files, 351 MB, served through
# functions/data/browse/[[path]].js. As with data/graph above, this exclusion is
# what MAKES that Function run -- a deployed static copy would shadow it.
data/browse/

# Dublin development-plan scans. No Function needed: every reference to these in
# the catalogue is already an absolute https://data.civgraph.net/ URL, so R2 is
# where the site sends people regardless. All 12 verified byte-exact in the
# bucket on 2026-08-12.
data/documents/
# Timeline transition full analysis sidecars are source QA; runtime uses data/timeline-transition-overlays/
data/timeline-transitions/

data/maps/**/*.fgb
data/maps/**/*.fgb.gz
data/maps/**/*-chunks.json
data/maps/osni-originals/

# /test MapLibre tile payloads are served from R2/CDN as PMTiles in production.
# Directory MVT pyramids are local build/fallback artifacts and must not count
# against the Cloudflare Pages deployment file limit.
render/tiles/
render/pmtiles/generated/
node_modules/

# --- Not served by the site; excluded to stay under the Pages 20,000-file limit ---
# The deployment was measured at ~20,944 files on 2026-08-03, i.e. over the ceiling.
#
# Root election-viewer-package/ is the pre-app copy of the standalone viewer. Its only
# consumer is js/election-controller.js, which no HTML file loads (the js/ Leaflet stack
# is dead legacy). The live site loads app/election-viewer-package/ instead -- six CSS/JS
# files, no data directory -- so the leading slash below is load-bearing: unanchored,
# this pattern would match the app copy too and take the election viewer's styles with it.
/election-viewer-package/

# Working analysis, not site content.
analysis/

# Pipeline inputs: alignment CSVs, corrections and official-result sources consumed by
# scripts at build time. Nothing under app/src or render/src fetches them.
data/elections/

# Card thumbnail images are served from R2 (https://data.civgraph.net/assets/thumbnails/)
# via js/cdn-url.js. They stay in git as the source of truth; they just do not need to
# occupy 1,793 of the Pages file budget to be delivered.
#
# Only the images are excluded. manifest.json stays in the deploy because
# build-shared-shell-assets.mjs regenerates it from this directory on every build --
# serving it from R2 as well would let the list and the images drift apart.
#
# After adding or re-rendering a thumbnail, run: npm run sync:thumbnails
# (idempotent; it skips objects already present).
assets/thumbnails/*.webp
assets/thumbnails/*.png

# R2 publication allowlist — governs what may be written to the public bucket.
# Operational config, not site content: publishing it would hand out a map of
# the bucket's prefix layout for no benefit to any reader.
data/database/r2-publication-allowlist.json
